{"lines": ["One steamship stopped miles from the sinking Titanic, watched eight white rockets, and never moved to help.", "On April fourteenth, nineteen twelve, Captain Stanley Lord stopped the steamer Californian at an Atlantic ice field. Her lone radio operator switched off his set and went to bed.", "After midnight, Second Officer Herbert Stone watched a nearby steamer fire white rockets, eight in all. He said a ship does not fire rockets at sea for nothing.", "Yet Captain Lord told his men to keep using the Morse lamp. The radio stayed off until after four-thirty, when the Titanic had already sunk.", "The British inquiry said the Californian might have saved many, if not all, of the lives lost.", "Lord claimed a smaller third ship fired the rockets. A U.S. Navy hydrographer found no third ship in the area.", "Eight white rockets. A radio switched off. Nobody explained it."], "words": [["One", 0.0, 0.18], ["steamship", 0.18, 0.78], ["stopped", 0.78, 1.1], ["miles", 1.1, 1.5], ["from", 1.5, 1.96], ["the", 1.96, 2.08], ["sinking", 2.08, 2.32], ["Titanic,", 2.32, 2.7], ["watched", 3.34, 3.62], ["eight", 3.62, 4.08], ["white", 4.08, 4.38], ["rockets,", 4.38, 4.76], ["and", 5.2, 5.4], ["never", 5.4, 5.64], ["moved", 5.64, 6.0], ["to", 6.0, 6.16], ["help.", 6.16, 6.36], ["On", 6.82, 6.88], ["April", 6.88, 7.08], ["fourteenth,", 7.08, 7.713], ["nineteen", 7.713, 8.22], ["twelve,", 8.22, 8.6], ["Captain", 9.0, 9.38], ["Stanley", 9.38, 9.7], ["Lord", 9.7, 10.1], ["stopped", 10.1, 10.44], ["the", 10.44, 10.66], ["steamer", 10.66, 10.94], ["Californian", 10.94, 11.66], ["at", 11.66, 11.86], ["an", 11.86, 11.96], ["Atlantic", 11.96, 12.2], ["ice", 12.2, 12.66], ["field.", 12.66, 12.94], ["Her", 13.54, 13.58], ["lone", 13.58, 13.74], ["radio", 13.74, 14.12], ["operator", 14.12, 14.56], ["switched", 14.56, 14.94], ["off", 14.94, 15.26], ["his", 15.26, 15.4], ["set", 15.4, 15.64], ["and", 15.64, 15.82], ["went", 15.82, 16.0], ["to", 16.0, 16.16], ["bed.", 16.16, 16.36], ["After